---
/**
 * Fender neck dates spoke, CONDENSED REBUILD, preview build.
 *
 * Hub-and-spoke method page behind the condensed Fender serial rebuild
 * (see fender-serial-hub-preview.astro). Deep-dives the neck heel date method
 * the hub only summarizes, so the hub's "/fender-neck-dates/" card resolves.
 *
 * Noindex + sitemap-excluded + X-Robots-Tag (astro.config.mjs SITEMAP_EXCLUDE
 * and public/_headers), same preview pattern as the hub, /fender-pot-codes/,
 * and /fender-serial-tool-v2/.
 *
 * Core content and photos come from Joe's live serial page (the "Neck Heel
 * Dates" section of /fender-guitars-serial-number-guide/). Facts trace to
 * VG_FACTS.md (joes-vintage-databases): VG-0051 (neck date = penciled/stamped
 * on the heel, marked until ~1976, penciled until March 1962) and VG-0055 (the
 * neck heel date is the single most reliable dating clue).
 *
 * The Green Stamp section draws on GGJaguar's 1969-1971 CBS neck-code reference
 * (ggjaguar.com/neckcode.htm): green ink, 6-8 digits read outside-in as model,
 * batch, month, year, width; runs alongside the plain date stamp; hard to read.
 * The Neck Stamp Model Codes table (the model prefix, 1 to 28) is Joe-supplied
 * CBS-era reference data, refined per Joe: code 2 = Strat into early 1968 (not to
 * 1965), code 13 = Telecaster (1967-1968), code 3 = mainly Esquire. Green stamp,
 * model codes, and reissue detail are not yet in VG_FACTS; flagged to log.
 *
 * MODEL CODES, CORRECTED 2026-07-20 (Joe approved after seeing the evidence).
 * THE KEY FACT: Fender RENUMBERED the model codes at the end of 1965, so one
 * model has different codes in different years. Strat = 2 (1962-65) -> 13
 * (1966-68) -> 22 (1968-72); Jaguar = 1 (1962-65) -> 15 (1966-72). The old table
 * had 13 = Telecaster and stretched codes 1 and 2 to "early 1968", which made
 * Jaguar appear at BOTH 1 and 15 for 1966-68 (a self-contradiction) and left no
 * code for a 1966-67 Strat. guitarhq's 1966 Strat page states the 2 -> 13 change
 * verbatim with the 2MAY65B / 13MAY66B example; a photographed Jan 1967 Strat
 * heel begins 13; no documented "2"-prefix stamp with a 66/67 year was found.
 * 13 = Telecaster ONLY in the separate 1972-1980 8-digit system - that cross-era
 * collision is the likely origin of the old error. Code 3 necessarily became
 * "Telecaster and Esquire" since Teles could no longer "move to 13".
 * The rest of Joe's 24-code table (5 = P-Bass, 6 = Bass VI, 8/9 = student
 * models, 10-28) was independently CONFIRMED and must be kept.
 *
 * REISSUE MARKINGS, CORRECTED 2026-07-20 (Joe approved after seeing the
 * evidence). Supersedes BOTH the earlier "Fullerton ink 1982-84 then Corona
 * pencil 1986 on" split AND an intermediate "1982 = black ink stamp" edit.
 * Fullerton AVRI necks (1982 to the plant closing end of 1984) carry a GRAPHITE
 * PENCIL date in numeric M-D-YY; pencil ran to ~1988, when black ink stamps with
 * 3-letter months began. Photographed examples: 5-11-82, 12-24-82, 5-27-82,
 * 1-14-83, 11-03-83; earliest Corona-era 11-1-85 (Corona opened Oct 1985, NOT
 * 1986). The ink stamps genuinely present on Fullerton heels are the BUILDER /
 * INSPECTOR NAME (e.g. H. Gastelum, J. Torres) and the word VINTAGE, neither of
 * which is a date - that is what makes people call these necks ink-stamped.
 * Some 1982 necks carry no date at all.
 */
