  ["#appraisal", "Free Expert Appraisal"],
  ["#about-joe", "About Joe"],
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Do I Have To Take The Neck Off To Read The Date?",
    a: "Yes. The date is on the butt of the heel, tucked inside the neck pocket, so the neck has to come off the body. It is four screws on the neck plate, but vintage necks and finishes chip easily. If you aren't comfortable doing that, don't force it. Get in touch and I'll help, or bring the guitar by and I'll read it for you.",
  },
  {
    q: "My Neck Date Is Older Than My Serial Number. Is That A Problem?",
    a: "Usually not. Fender kept finished necks in bins and pulled them out of order, so a neck a few months, even a year or two, older than the build is common and original. A neck dated well after the rest of the guitar is the real red flag.",
  },
  {
    q: "There's No Date On My Neck Heel. Why?",
    a: "A few reasons, and one of them isn't a fault at all. Fender deliberately stopped penciling heel dates for a window in mid to late 1959, around the time the slab rosewood board arrived, and resumed in 1960, so a genuine 1959 neck can come out blank. Beyond that, heel marking got patchy through the mid 1970s as serial numbers moved to the headstock decal. A pencil date can also wear off or get sanded away in a refret or refinish, or it's there but too faint to see. Send me a clear photo of the heel in raking light and I'll tell you what's there.",
  },
  {
    q: "What Does The Letter On The Ink Stamp Mean?",
    a: "The final letter on a 1960s neck stamp is the nut width, not a date. A is narrow (1 1/2 inch), B is standard (1 5/8 inch), C is wide (1 3/4 inch), and D is extra wide (1 7/8 inch). It won't date the neck, but it is a useful originality check against the guitar in your hands.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does The Neck Date Prove My Guitar Is All Original?",
    a: "No. It dates the neck. Originality is a whole-guitar judgment that weighs the body date, the pot codes, the pickups, the hardware, and the finish together. Send me three photos and I'll give you the real story for free.",
  },
];

// ---- Schema ----
const articleSchema = {
